course: dictionary
lesson: 265
title: Amazing and stronger words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Amazing means very surprising and wonderful, so something that makes you stop and wonder. «Eagles are big birds of prey: hunters with hooked beaks, huge feet and amazing eyes.» Here amazing tells you the eyes are remarkable, the sort that make you look twice.
explain: In everyday talk, amazing also means very good or excellent, as in an amazing film. It comes from the verb amaze, so a thing that amazes you is amazing. The adverb is amazingly, which tells you how something happens.
explain: Because people use amazing for so many things, it can become a tired word. Writers often choose a stronger, more exact word: astonishing, breathtaking, incredible or spectacular. Each one shows a slightly different amount of wonder.
explain: Check facts before you call something amazing. «Some tales are nearly true, like the owl that turns its head "all the way round"; it turns about three-quarters of the way, and that is amazing enough.» The owl is amazing, but the tale stretches the truth, so read carefully.
fact: Amazing means very surprising and wonderful, causing great wonder.
fact: In everyday speech, amazing can mean very good or excellent, as in an amazing film.
fact: Amazingly is the adverb form, and it tells you how something happens.
fact: Stronger choices for amazing include astonishing, breathtaking, incredible and spectacular.
fact: «Frogs live on every continent except Antarctica, and they come in amazing shapes.»
exercise: «Eagles are big birds of prey with amazing eyes.» What does amazing mean here? | Small and round | Very cold and wet | *Very surprising and wonderful | Sleepy and slow
exercise: Kai says the new game is amazing. What does he probably mean? | It is quiet and boring | It is made of a strange metal | It was made a very long time ago | *It is excellent and great fun
exercise: Which word is a stronger, more exact choice than amazing for a view from a mountain top? | Nice | Okay | *Breathtaking | Fine
test: Which word is the adverb form of amazing? | amaze | amazement | *amazingly | amazed
test: Mia's story amazed the class. Which word is the verb? | story | Mia's | class | *amazed
exam: Which use of amazing means excellent, like praise? | The amazing bridge was built in 1920 | Amazing has seven letters | Lila lost her amazing bag | *Kai said the film was amazing, the best he has seen
